  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Guidehouse has $718M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, recorded across 334 awards with an average award size of $2.1M. Obligations are up 32.8% year over year. Guidehouse received obligations from a wide set of agencies, led by the Department of Defense with $146M and the Department of the Interior with $136M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest market by obligations at $338M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $164M and Other Accounting Services at $111M. Fiscal-year obligations show growth from $28.2M in FY21 to $718M in FY26, with prior-year peaks at $761M in FY24 and $631M in FY23. The FY2026 totals are partial, fiscal year to date. This profile highlights where Guidehouse’s federal revenue is concentrated by agency and NAICS market and provides a snapshot of current-year scale and market mix for business development and capture planning.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Guidehouse's largest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $146M in obligations. The Department of the Interior follows with $136M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $107M. Six other agencies each account for seven-figure obligations, including the Department of Health and Human Services with $81.4M and the Department of Justice with $77.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which service areas drive Guidehouse's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest market at $338M. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Accounting Services are the next largest markets at $164M and $111M respectively. Engineering Services, Custom Computer Programming Services, and a set of smaller professional services together account for the remaining listed obligations."
      }
    ]
